1
00:00:04,137 --> 00:00:10,010
When you get to my level, hands move
on their own at such simple surgeries.

2
00:00:11,578 --> 00:00:14,047
Maybe you don't understand

3
00:00:14,848 --> 00:00:19,686
but I call this a "in the zone" feeling.

4
00:00:21,287 --> 00:00:22,122
Hey, Arima.

5
00:00:22,255 --> 00:00:23,189
I'm sorry.

6
00:00:27,360 --> 00:00:28,395
Like this?

7
00:00:28,461 --> 00:00:31,798
BP dropped. 75 over 48.
Adding ringer's solution.

8
00:00:32,065 --> 00:00:34,634
Dr. Jonouchi, OR 3 is ready to begin.

9
00:00:34,701 --> 00:00:37,670
I can't leave.
I'll be there when I finish.

10
00:00:37,737 --> 00:00:38,972
They're in a hurry.

11
00:00:39,039 --> 00:00:41,007
I only have one body.

12
00:00:41,074 --> 00:00:44,677
I started having this feeling
10 years ago.

13
00:00:44,744 --> 00:00:47,047
I was appointed by a politician.

14
00:00:47,213 --> 00:00:49,749
The surgery was artistic.

15
00:00:50,984 --> 00:00:53,086
Too bright.
We're not taking photos.

16
00:00:53,453 --> 00:00:54,287
I'm sorry.

17
00:00:54,421 --> 00:00:55,388
Monopolar.

18
00:00:55,455 --> 00:00:58,191
I'm worried about blood loss.
Check the operative field.

19
00:00:58,458 --> 00:00:59,826
Shut up.

20
00:00:59,926 --> 00:01:02,295
Don't interrupt me.
You're just an anesthesiologist.

21
00:01:04,130 --> 00:01:06,933
This doesn't come from experience.

22
00:01:07,067 --> 00:01:08,968
It's a surgeon's outstanding instinct.

23
00:01:09,102 --> 00:01:12,072
I have no one to share this feeling.

24
00:01:13,673 --> 00:01:14,908
Makes me feel empty at times...

25
00:01:14,974 --> 00:01:16,209
So annoying.

26
00:01:16,342 --> 00:01:18,578
He brags so his surgeries take forever.

27
00:01:18,645 --> 00:01:19,479
And not good.

28
00:01:19,546 --> 00:01:22,082
I can't stand the way
he looks down on anesthesiologists.

29
00:01:22,215 --> 00:01:23,216
Such an annoying man.

30
00:01:23,850 --> 00:01:28,188
They're undermanned so they make me do
multiple surgeries at a time.

31
00:01:28,455 --> 00:01:31,791
If I were you, I don't mind doing
many surgeries.

32
00:01:32,058 --> 00:01:34,861
Michiko and Hiromi.
Here you are.

33
00:01:35,228 --> 00:01:36,663
Let's eat.

34
00:01:41,701 --> 00:01:46,940
You'll take care of my wife
so eat and get your energy.

35
00:01:47,574 --> 00:01:50,477
Your gyoza dumplings are
the best in the world.

36
00:01:50,543 --> 00:01:51,878
Good and fast.

37
00:01:51,945 --> 00:01:54,747
I'm glad your wife gets to
have her surgery early.

38
00:01:54,881 --> 00:01:57,117
It's not a major surgery

39
00:01:57,283 --> 00:01:59,786
but I'm grateful you two will perform it.

40
00:02:01,421 --> 00:02:03,590
We're good and fast.

41
00:02:04,124 --> 00:02:06,326
That's encouraging. Thank you.

42
00:02:09,362 --> 00:02:10,196
What's wrong?

43
00:02:11,631 --> 00:02:14,601
I have a little stomachache.

44
00:02:14,734 --> 00:02:15,702
Hmm.

45
00:02:39,092 --> 00:02:42,128
KAGENOBU UCHIKANDA
THE LEADER OF THE MEDICAL WORLD

46
00:02:57,410 --> 00:02:59,012
Only Dr. Nishiyama is here?

47
00:02:59,212 --> 00:03:01,114
- Yes. What's the matter?
- Well...

48
00:03:03,183 --> 00:03:04,017
What?

49
00:03:04,350 --> 00:03:05,218
What?

50
00:03:05,351 --> 00:03:06,619
Why are you eating?

51
00:03:06,719 --> 00:03:07,587
Why?

52
00:03:07,654 --> 00:03:11,324
You already ate three.
That's the forth one.

53
00:03:11,391 --> 00:03:14,227
I thought you didn't want to
eat anymore.

54
00:03:14,394 --> 00:03:16,796
Yeah, I don't mind.

55
00:03:17,964 --> 00:03:21,000
- Your phone is ringing.
- Yes, yes.

56
00:03:23,469 --> 00:03:24,604
Hello?

57
00:03:24,671 --> 00:03:28,541
You said I can go back to
work right after the surgery.

58
00:03:28,675 --> 00:03:32,111
My right leg is swollen
so I can barely walk.

59
00:03:34,013 --> 00:03:35,215
I'm really sorry.

60
00:03:37,450 --> 00:03:41,321
The surgery took longer
than I thought.

61
00:03:41,387 --> 00:03:44,390
The next election will be a tough one.

62
00:03:44,591 --> 00:03:47,093
My supporters are waiting.

63
00:03:50,396 --> 00:03:51,698
To tell the truth,

64
00:03:52,498 --> 00:03:57,770
the anesthesiologist was a bit inefficient
and that affected your body.

65
00:03:57,904 --> 00:03:59,539
What are you talking about?

66
00:03:59,672 --> 00:04:01,040
Jonouchi.

67
00:04:01,674 --> 00:04:04,310
You have to apologize to Mr. Tamaki.

68
00:04:04,644 --> 00:04:06,613
You did a slow job, right?

69
00:04:06,746 --> 00:04:07,614
You're rude!

70
00:04:08,815 --> 00:04:12,485
We have people's lives
in our hands.

71
00:04:12,685 --> 00:04:14,087
No excuses.

72
00:04:15,622 --> 00:04:17,323
That's why
I don't like part-timers.

73
00:04:17,890 --> 00:04:20,593
We'll consider her punishment.

74
00:04:21,694 --> 00:04:24,330
I understand. Bye.

75
00:04:25,064 --> 00:04:26,633
What did he say?

76
00:04:27,267 --> 00:04:30,703
Hiromi, you're banned from Totei
University Hospital for awhile.

77
00:04:30,770 --> 00:04:34,474
University hospitals are swift
in such instances.

78
00:04:34,540 --> 00:04:36,843
That annoying man set you up.

79
00:04:37,543 --> 00:04:39,812
Isn't there a way to seek
revenge against him?

80
00:04:40,046 --> 00:04:43,049
The patient is a politician
so it's troublesome.

81
00:04:43,383 --> 00:04:46,252
I'll find another hospital for you.
Just wait.

82
00:04:46,486 --> 00:04:50,890
I still need money for Mai.
I'll be in trouble if my income decreases.

83
00:04:51,658 --> 00:04:55,028
Can't you reduce the margin on commission?

84
00:04:55,094 --> 00:04:56,496
- Commission?
- Hiromi.

85
00:04:57,196 --> 00:04:59,499
Does Dr. Jonouchi operate
on a commission system?

86
00:05:00,667 --> 00:05:03,036
I didn't know that.
I'm paid by salary.

87
00:05:03,102 --> 00:05:06,572
It doesn't matter
how many surgeries I performed.

88
00:05:06,639 --> 00:05:09,208
You don't even negotiate,
you're simply dumb.

89
00:05:09,442 --> 00:05:13,479
You always perform selfish surgery,
so it's natural your pay is less.

90
00:05:13,546 --> 00:05:15,148
Selfish surgery?

91
00:05:15,214 --> 00:05:17,884
Ben Casey, what do you want?

92
00:05:17,950 --> 00:05:21,054
Do you have a stomachache?
Come here.

93
00:05:21,254 --> 00:05:23,222
You always change methods.

94
00:05:23,289 --> 00:05:25,725
Do you ever care how tough it is for us?

95
00:05:25,792 --> 00:05:27,860
You ate my gyoza.

96
00:05:28,027 --> 00:05:30,129
Gyoza? What are you talking about?

97
00:05:30,196 --> 00:05:31,798
It shows your selfishness.

98
00:05:31,864 --> 00:05:33,333
You didn't eat it so I did.

99
00:05:33,399 --> 00:05:35,568
I like to eat
my favorite food last.

100
00:05:35,635 --> 00:05:39,272
Next time, you'd better eat it first.

101
00:05:40,073 --> 00:05:43,242
By the way, how much do you get?

102
00:05:43,309 --> 00:05:44,744
Let me go!

103
00:05:44,811 --> 00:05:45,812
Too much power!

104
00:05:45,945 --> 00:05:49,549
Too much power? You're fired!

105
00:05:51,351 --> 00:05:55,054
This is the story of
a lone wolf woman doctor.

106
00:06:08,501 --> 00:06:12,572
You'll work as my anesthesiologist
throughout my surgeries.

107
00:06:13,039 --> 00:06:14,207
You got it?

108
00:06:14,374 --> 00:06:15,475
Yes sir.

109
00:06:16,075 --> 00:06:19,912
You should have assigned me
instead of that part-timer.

110
00:06:20,046 --> 00:06:24,117
She blamed me for her fault.
What a daring part-timer.

111
00:06:24,250 --> 00:06:26,886
A part-timer is
a part-timer anyway.

112
00:06:27,320 --> 00:06:29,822
You're right. A part-timer is
just a part-timer.

113
00:06:30,690 --> 00:06:32,058
<i>In 2017</i>

114
00:06:32,492 --> 00:06:37,363
<i>the university medical system</i>
<i>regained its once-lost authority</i>

115
00:06:37,697 --> 00:06:43,336
<i>and the system on which lives depend</i>
<i>strayed away from what it should be.</i>

116
00:06:43,469 --> 00:06:46,439
The director isn't here so he feels like
he's the acting director.

117
00:06:46,639 --> 00:06:48,708
No, he thinks he's the director.

118
00:06:50,410 --> 00:06:55,081
<i>In the midst of this, doctors free</i>
<i>from any establishment emerged.</i>

119
00:06:55,381 --> 00:06:59,285
<i>Freelance doctors, in other words,</i>
<i>lone wolf doctors.</i>

120
00:07:01,220 --> 00:07:02,889
<i>This woman, for example.</i>

121
00:07:03,523 --> 00:07:07,593
<i>Despising the herd mentality, authority</i>
<i>and institutional restraints...</i>

122
00:07:07,927 --> 00:07:13,266
<i>Her solo weapons are her license</i>
<i>and the skills she has acquired.</i>

123
00:07:15,201 --> 00:07:17,470
<i>Surgeon Michiko Daimon.</i>

124
00:07:17,937 --> 00:07:19,038
<i>Also known as...</i>

125
00:07:19,539 --> 00:07:21,207
<i>Doctor-X.</i>

126
00:07:43,329 --> 00:07:47,633
Dr. Torii was suspended
because of his revolt

127
00:07:48,367 --> 00:07:50,503
at the press conference.

128
00:07:51,971 --> 00:07:56,209
He's completely dropped out from
the next chief surgeon nomination.

129
00:07:57,276 --> 00:08:01,214
But why are you sitting on the chair?

130
00:08:02,381 --> 00:08:03,249
Why?

131
00:08:03,950 --> 00:08:07,820
When the director is not here

132
00:08:08,354 --> 00:08:10,990
naturally I'm the acting director.

133
00:08:11,190 --> 00:08:12,492
- Naturally?
- Yes.

134
00:08:14,193 --> 00:08:15,394
Director!

135
00:08:15,995 --> 00:08:18,397
Hey, I'm still Acting Director.

136
00:08:18,464 --> 00:08:19,432
Do you remember?

137
00:08:19,732 --> 00:08:21,534
This one? You wanted the wallet.

138
00:08:21,667 --> 00:08:23,236
- Yes!
- Wait.

139
00:08:23,536 --> 00:08:25,938
Did you report to the director?

140
00:08:26,072 --> 00:08:30,776
I did. The part-timer anesthesiologist
caused a problem at the hospital,

141
00:08:30,843 --> 00:08:36,082
but Dr. Inomata handled it swiftly
and saved the hospital.

142
00:08:36,148 --> 00:08:37,283
Good job!

143
00:08:38,117 --> 00:08:39,952
- Good girl.
- I love it!

144
00:08:47,026 --> 00:08:49,228
A leader

145
00:08:50,329 --> 00:08:52,832
needs to have something
better than others.

146
00:08:54,166 --> 00:08:57,103
Dr. Ebina, what do you have?

147
00:08:59,372 --> 00:09:05,011
What…do…you…have?

148
00:09:06,812 --> 00:09:07,813
Huh?

149
00:09:09,348 --> 00:09:11,217
Huh?

150
00:09:15,955 --> 00:09:17,323
Excuse me.

151
00:09:17,857 --> 00:09:19,025
Michiko.

152
00:09:19,091 --> 00:09:20,993
You came.

153
00:09:21,060 --> 00:09:23,062
Today we're closed.

154
00:09:23,129 --> 00:09:23,963
I see.

155
00:09:27,099 --> 00:09:28,467
What're you doing?

156
00:09:29,235 --> 00:09:30,937
- Visiting.
- Really.

157
00:09:31,237 --> 00:09:35,942
I heard Hiromi can't do
Atsuko's surgery.

158
00:09:37,043 --> 00:09:38,544
That's too bad.

159
00:09:39,378 --> 00:09:42,515
That anesthesiologist is selfish
so she was fired.

160
00:09:42,815 --> 00:09:44,450
Who is selfish?

161
00:09:45,651 --> 00:09:47,820
A squabble? That's unusual.

162
00:09:49,288 --> 00:09:51,090
Because of my gyoza.

163
00:09:53,092 --> 00:09:55,361
Anyway I'm counting on you.

164
00:09:55,761 --> 00:09:58,497
I want her to
come back home ASAP.

165
00:09:58,965 --> 00:10:03,669
I know you're busy so you don't
have to come here everyday.

166
00:10:03,970 --> 00:10:06,472
I'm okay.

167
00:10:06,539 --> 00:10:08,841
Want to eat some apple
Hiromi has brought?

168
00:10:10,543 --> 00:10:13,112
Can she eat a little bit?

169
00:10:13,713 --> 00:10:14,547
Go ahead.

170
00:10:14,647 --> 00:10:15,781
- Thank you.
- I told you.

171
00:10:26,626 --> 00:10:29,695
Just a moment. I'll peel the apple.

172
00:10:40,106 --> 00:10:40,973
Mr. Mutsuura?

173
00:10:41,841 --> 00:10:43,409
I'm okay. It's nothing.

174
00:10:43,476 --> 00:10:45,378
Let's do a check up.

175
00:10:45,811 --> 00:10:46,779
Come on.

176
00:10:46,846 --> 00:10:48,714
CT ROOM

177
00:11:08,934 --> 00:11:10,269
IPMN.

178
00:11:11,003 --> 00:11:13,005
The main pancreatic duct expanded.

179
00:11:13,139 --> 00:11:15,007
The head of the pancreas
may be malignant.

180
00:11:15,074 --> 00:11:17,009
Complicated with acute pancreatitis.

181
00:11:17,943 --> 00:11:19,045
Radical resection?

182
00:11:19,111 --> 00:11:22,682
It may cause malignant transformation
and he might die.

183
00:11:23,949 --> 00:11:28,521
What a troublesome case
during the director's absence.

184
00:11:30,756 --> 00:11:33,125
His wife will also have
surgery soon, right?

185
00:11:33,192 --> 00:11:34,060
Yes.

186
00:11:34,293 --> 00:11:35,895
I'm sorry for the couple.

187
00:11:36,395 --> 00:11:37,263
Right? Dr. Daimon.

188
00:11:39,765 --> 00:11:41,100
Dr. Inomata.

189
00:11:41,901 --> 00:11:42,868
Can I?

190
00:11:43,302 --> 00:11:44,170
Excuse me.

191
00:11:46,405 --> 00:11:51,811
I'd like to introduce you to
a post-surgery treatment on the patient.

192
00:11:51,877 --> 00:11:55,381
We can have a strong connection
with a company.

193
00:11:55,481 --> 00:11:57,116
With a suitable reward.

194
00:11:57,717 --> 00:11:59,051
Reward?

195
00:11:59,552 --> 00:12:02,621
No, no. Rewards are not good.

196
00:12:02,755 --> 00:12:06,959
But maybe the director will be happy.

197
00:12:07,393 --> 00:12:13,032
When you do, please mention my name.
Acting Director.

198
00:12:13,099 --> 00:12:13,933
No!

199
00:12:14,767 --> 00:12:15,735
Next director.

200
00:12:16,035 --> 00:12:19,238
Hey, hey.
I don't have ambition.

201
00:12:19,472 --> 00:12:20,506
No ambition.

202
00:12:22,041 --> 00:12:26,512
You certainly are an anesthesiologist
packed with worldly wisdom.

203
00:12:27,246 --> 00:12:29,348
You are totally different
from the part-timer.

204
00:12:37,723 --> 00:12:39,792
IPMN?

205
00:12:41,894 --> 00:12:44,930
Multiple pancreatic tumors.

206
00:12:46,265 --> 00:12:47,733
Maybe malignant.

207
00:12:53,272 --> 00:12:55,608
Am I going to die?

208
00:12:55,741 --> 00:12:56,809
No, we won't let you die.

209
00:12:56,942 --> 00:12:58,677
Let me do your surgery.

210
00:12:58,944 --> 00:13:01,280
We need to remove your pancreas.

211
00:13:01,347 --> 00:13:04,250
You can live with hormone replacement
on a daily basis.

212
00:13:06,719 --> 00:13:10,022
Can I continue to work
in such a condition?

213
00:13:11,824 --> 00:13:15,628
After the surgery
you need time to adjust to the insulin.

214
00:13:17,830 --> 00:13:18,664
I see.

215
00:13:33,279 --> 00:13:35,748
I hope he doesn't need to remove it.

216
00:13:35,815 --> 00:13:39,018
But it's tough under his condition.

217
00:13:39,952 --> 00:13:44,523
His wife's surgery isn't difficult
but I worry because she does dialysis.

218
00:13:46,425 --> 00:13:47,359
Dr. Daimon...

219
00:13:49,094 --> 00:13:52,498
Regarding vascular treatment,
what should I be careful about?

220
00:13:53,465 --> 00:13:54,967
Are you going to be an assistant?

221
00:13:55,434 --> 00:13:59,138
Yes, I'm preparing for the surgery.

222
00:14:06,979 --> 00:14:10,783
A dialysis patient needs
perfect hemostasis during surgery.

223
00:14:10,983 --> 00:14:13,986
And you have to
ligate the renal veins first.

224
00:14:15,487 --> 00:14:16,555
Thank you.

225
00:14:20,626 --> 00:14:22,228
I don't like her.

226
00:14:23,295 --> 00:14:26,799
Her attitude is bad and
she uses us too hard.

227
00:14:27,399 --> 00:14:31,003
Since Dr. Daimon has been here,
all you think about is surgery.

228
00:14:33,005 --> 00:14:34,473
Getting enough sleep lately?

229
00:14:35,274 --> 00:14:36,108
Yes.

230
00:14:40,012 --> 00:14:41,146
Oh, Nishiyama.

231
00:14:45,084 --> 00:14:47,720
You are the second assistant
for Mrs. Mutsuura's surgery?

232
00:14:48,120 --> 00:14:50,222
- Yes.
- I'll be the first assistant.

233
00:14:51,924 --> 00:14:53,592
Let's go drink before the surgery.

234
00:14:56,996 --> 00:14:59,031
You want to join us?

235
00:14:59,865 --> 00:15:01,367
- Sure.
- Good.

236
00:15:06,538 --> 00:15:08,574
We do nothing during
Dr. Daimon's surgery.

237
00:15:08,908 --> 00:15:10,643
She does everything by herself.

238
00:15:10,743 --> 00:15:13,512
Dr. Daimon is great, isn't she?

239
00:15:13,879 --> 00:15:15,948
She is great but she bothers us.

240
00:15:16,949 --> 00:15:17,950
Nishiyama...

241
00:15:18,484 --> 00:15:20,486
Hm? Did I ask this before?

242
00:15:20,886 --> 00:15:21,854
Why become a surgeon?

243
00:15:23,188 --> 00:15:25,124
I can do surgery.

244
00:15:25,958 --> 00:15:27,126
That's the only reason.

245
00:15:27,559 --> 00:15:28,427
Cool.

246
00:15:28,994 --> 00:15:30,262
Really cool.

247
00:15:31,030 --> 00:15:32,298
But you have to be careful.

248
00:15:32,731 --> 00:15:37,236
If you become like her,
you'll have no place in the hospital.

249
00:15:37,670 --> 00:15:39,838
Can I have another beer?

250
00:15:39,972 --> 00:15:40,806
Sure.

251
00:15:41,373 --> 00:15:42,474
I don't need a place in the hospital.

252
00:15:43,409 --> 00:15:44,376
Huh?

253
00:15:44,743 --> 00:15:45,611
Nothing.

254
00:15:46,979 --> 00:15:50,749
But Dr. Inomata's way is no good either.

255
00:15:51,083 --> 00:15:53,352
Nobody will follow him.

256
00:15:53,619 --> 00:15:56,355
What is this "in the zone" feeling
he told us about?

257
00:15:56,822 --> 00:16:00,192
He said "My hands move on their own
when I'm in the zone.

258
00:16:00,292 --> 00:16:03,529
If they do, it's in the danger zone."

259
00:16:03,662 --> 00:16:09,001
CHINESE GYOZA

260
00:16:10,202 --> 00:16:12,204
CLOSED UNTIL FURTHER NOTICE

261
00:16:13,605 --> 00:16:15,140
Good evening.

262
00:16:15,874 --> 00:16:17,543
Mr. Mutsuura?

263
00:16:20,846 --> 00:16:21,914
Oh, Hiromi.

264
00:16:22,881 --> 00:16:25,117
Why do you look so depressed?

265
00:16:26,018 --> 00:16:27,586
Did you hear about me?

266
00:16:27,886 --> 00:16:28,887
Yes.

267
00:16:29,755 --> 00:16:35,394
I'm banned from the hospital but
if there's anything I can do for you...

268
00:16:35,627 --> 00:16:38,430
Thanks but I'm okay.

269
00:16:40,466 --> 00:16:44,169
I have to do surgery ASAP
so I just came back here to get ready.

270
00:16:47,573 --> 00:16:50,175
Did you tell your wife about your illness?

271
00:16:51,043 --> 00:16:51,944
Um.

272
00:16:52,945 --> 00:16:55,614
I don't think I can hide it

273
00:16:56,181 --> 00:16:59,952
but I'll try until
her surgery is finished.

274
00:17:01,053 --> 00:17:05,124
I won't be able use the pan for a while.

275
00:17:05,958 --> 00:17:06,792
I don't know.

276
00:17:08,027 --> 00:17:09,361
What's going to happen next?

277
00:17:13,298 --> 00:17:16,402
I have to support my wife but...

278
00:17:17,669 --> 00:17:21,273
If I need somebody's help

279
00:17:23,108 --> 00:17:25,844
then what will become of us?

280
00:17:40,626 --> 00:17:44,363
First case.
Atsuko Mutsuura, 62 years old.

281
00:17:44,496 --> 00:17:46,698
Kidney cancer that occurred
under dialysis.

282
00:17:47,633 --> 00:17:50,069
Dr. Daimon will be the surgeon.

283
00:17:50,436 --> 00:17:53,005
Yes. Right nephrectomy.

284
00:17:53,072 --> 00:17:55,007
Such a minor surgery.

285
00:17:56,241 --> 00:17:57,209
Second case.

286
00:17:57,443 --> 00:17:59,711
Yoshio Mutsuura, 62 years old.

287
00:18:00,379 --> 00:18:01,580
IPMN.

288
00:18:01,947 --> 00:18:05,484
The tumor in the head of the pancreas
may be malignant.

289
00:18:05,551 --> 00:18:07,219
This case is a tough one.

290
00:18:08,353 --> 00:18:10,923
It requires a very difficult operation.

291
00:18:12,391 --> 00:18:15,494
We can't fail during
the director's absence.

292
00:18:16,462 --> 00:18:21,467
By pancreaticoduodenectomy
we resect the big tumor.

293
00:18:21,600 --> 00:18:24,803
Then we do chemotherapy.

294
00:18:25,170 --> 00:18:26,605
That's the best way.

295
00:18:28,307 --> 00:18:29,508
Objection.

296
00:18:30,209 --> 00:18:31,944
It can't be cured that way.

297
00:18:32,211 --> 00:18:34,780
The main pancreatic duct
has also expanded.

298
00:18:35,013 --> 00:18:37,049
There's a high risk of pancreatic cancer.

299
00:18:39,284 --> 00:18:40,152
I agree.

300
00:18:40,719 --> 00:18:44,623
With chemotherapy, we can't be sure
of its effect right away.

301
00:18:45,491 --> 00:18:47,493
So, it's far from the best way.

302
00:18:47,626 --> 00:18:49,094
Dr. Ebina.

303
00:18:49,261 --> 00:18:50,329
Finally.

304
00:18:50,395 --> 00:18:54,833
I'd like to ask, what is your best way?

305
00:18:56,335 --> 00:18:57,669
Well, I mean...

306
00:18:57,936 --> 00:18:58,770
You can do it!

307
00:18:58,837 --> 00:19:01,006
No way except a total removal.

308
00:19:01,974 --> 00:19:02,941
I agree.

309
00:19:03,542 --> 00:19:05,310
There's no way but a total removal.

310
00:19:05,744 --> 00:19:09,248
The patient's request is
keeping a high QOL.

311
00:19:09,815 --> 00:19:13,285
If the pancreas is completely removed,
he'll get diabetes.

312
00:19:14,553 --> 00:19:16,388
Either way he needs to
have the surgery.

313
00:19:16,522 --> 00:19:17,756
Either way?

314
00:19:19,191 --> 00:19:20,526
Are you stupid?

315
00:19:20,859 --> 00:19:23,462
What did you say?
Huh? What?

316
00:19:23,595 --> 00:19:25,898
Daimon is right.

317
00:19:26,465 --> 00:19:28,767
Your meager idea ignores the patient.

318
00:19:29,001 --> 00:19:29,968
Oh.

319
00:19:30,102 --> 00:19:31,637
Wow! Cool.

320
00:19:32,204 --> 00:19:33,972
I'm the acting director.

321
00:19:34,973 --> 00:19:36,441
You called me meager?!

322
00:19:36,508 --> 00:19:38,777
No, I didn't say that.

323
00:19:39,011 --> 00:19:40,312
I called the surgery meager.

324
00:19:40,445 --> 00:19:41,346
It's the same!

325
00:19:41,413 --> 00:19:43,115
Cut it out!
Continue this later.

326
00:19:43,182 --> 00:19:45,951
Anyway I'll perform the surgery.

327
00:19:47,152 --> 00:19:49,154
You can't handle this surgery.

328
00:19:49,688 --> 00:19:50,756
Huh?

329
00:19:51,056 --> 00:19:52,057
Because

330
00:19:53,225 --> 00:19:57,129
I already have the patient's approval
on my being his surgeon

331
00:19:58,463 --> 00:20:00,999
and the surgery method.

332
00:20:01,066 --> 00:20:03,969
CONSENT FORM

333
00:20:23,989 --> 00:20:24,823
Oh.

334
00:20:24,990 --> 00:20:25,891
Michiko.

335
00:20:26,992 --> 00:20:28,994
"The gyoza here is not bad, isn't it?"

336
00:20:29,161 --> 00:20:30,395
Yes, it's okay.

337
00:20:31,830 --> 00:20:35,467
Why let him do your surgery?

338
00:20:35,601 --> 00:20:39,938
Because he told me if I have the surgery,
I'll be able to work soon.

339
00:20:42,140 --> 00:20:46,511
The cost of medicine
after surgery is also cheaper.

340
00:20:46,845 --> 00:20:48,847
But you won't be cured.

341
00:20:48,914 --> 00:20:53,051
I don't want any obstacles
in my daily life after the surgery.

342
00:20:54,620 --> 00:20:57,189
I have to take care of
my restaurant and my wife.

343
00:20:58,257 --> 00:21:01,526
All the more reason to stay alive.

344
00:21:03,128 --> 00:21:03,962
Michiko.

345
00:21:05,931 --> 00:21:06,765
I...

346
00:21:08,200 --> 00:21:10,769
I don't want to be a burden
on my wife.

347
00:21:12,838 --> 00:21:15,741
It's better that I die quickly.

348
00:21:19,478 --> 00:21:21,513
Look at your face.

349
00:21:22,881 --> 00:21:26,451
I know you'll be happy
if I go back to work soon.

350
00:21:27,886 --> 00:21:33,358
I'll get back to work quickly
and let you eat my gyoza.

351
00:21:53,645 --> 00:21:58,150
What's this funny tension here?
A serious game going on?

352
00:21:58,817 --> 00:22:00,585
Or is there something wrong?

353
00:22:07,659 --> 00:22:08,760
Ron!

354
00:22:12,230 --> 00:22:15,767
If you want to say something,
just say it.

355
00:22:16,101 --> 00:22:18,070
This is not fun.

356
00:22:21,673 --> 00:22:22,607
Akira.

357
00:22:23,775 --> 00:22:27,813
I want Dr. Jonouchi
to be able to work at the hospital.

358
00:22:27,879 --> 00:22:29,014
Hiromi?

359
00:22:29,548 --> 00:22:30,882
I want to save Mr. Mutsuura.

360
00:22:31,216 --> 00:22:34,419
I heard Dr. Inomata will
perform the surgery.

361
00:22:34,553 --> 00:22:36,188
If that method is used,
Mr. Mutsuura will die.

362
00:22:36,421 --> 00:22:37,723
I have to do it.

363
00:22:39,257 --> 00:22:41,460
So you want Hiromi
to be the anesthesiologist?

364
00:22:42,260 --> 00:22:43,562
There is no one else.

365
00:22:44,696 --> 00:22:46,431
- I won't do it.
- Why?

366
00:22:46,665 --> 00:22:48,266
Mr. Mutsuura doesn't want to.

367
00:22:48,533 --> 00:22:50,502
You don't care if he dies?

368
00:22:50,669 --> 00:22:52,537
I didn't say so.

369
00:22:52,971 --> 00:22:55,240
But I understand how he feels.

370
00:22:58,276 --> 00:23:03,081
When I was sick,
I thought about Mai first.

371
00:23:03,348 --> 00:23:05,751
I didn't want to be a burden on Mai.

372
00:23:06,551 --> 00:23:10,222
It's natural to think about important
people in your life and hesitate.

373
00:23:10,956 --> 00:23:12,591
If you were a patient, you'd understand.

374
00:23:13,658 --> 00:23:17,262
And your surgery method is very risky.

375
00:23:18,096 --> 00:23:21,466
If we do surgery that
the patient doesn't want and fail,

376
00:23:21,833 --> 00:23:23,668
I'd be involved, too.

377
00:23:24,302 --> 00:23:25,771
I won't be able to feed Mai.

378
00:23:25,837 --> 00:23:26,905
I never fail.

379
00:23:28,273 --> 00:23:30,108
Maybe you won't fail

380
00:23:30,375 --> 00:23:33,845
but you want to do the surgery.
That's your choice.

381
00:23:34,212 --> 00:23:35,614
I can't keep up.

382
00:23:36,114 --> 00:23:37,549
Are you really a doctor?

383
00:23:41,787 --> 00:23:42,888
You're not a doctor.

384
00:23:45,724 --> 00:23:47,926
No way. I feel much better.
Let's play.

385
00:23:48,059 --> 00:23:50,896
Let's play, the three of us.

386
00:23:58,470 --> 00:24:00,872
YOSHIO MUTSUURA

387
00:24:03,875 --> 00:24:04,743
What?

388
00:24:07,179 --> 00:24:10,048
Will you let Dr. Inomata
perform the surgery?

389
00:24:10,816 --> 00:24:11,683
Huh?

390
00:24:12,451 --> 00:24:14,953
Did you reach your limit as a surgeon?

391
00:24:15,320 --> 00:24:16,288
Is that so?

392
00:24:17,556 --> 00:24:18,457
What's wrong?

393
00:24:19,558 --> 00:24:22,627
Not only is your face scary
but everything else too.

394
00:24:22,928 --> 00:24:23,895
Try to think more!

395
00:24:24,963 --> 00:24:26,498
There must be another option, right?

396
00:24:27,065 --> 00:24:30,135
A way to fulfill the patient's wish
and save his life as well.

397
00:24:31,002 --> 00:24:31,837
You have the option?

398
00:24:32,304 --> 00:24:33,238
Don't ask me.

399
00:24:37,843 --> 00:24:40,512
I've realized this is what
I'm better than others.

400
00:24:42,714 --> 00:24:46,651
For the hospital, for the patient,
I bring out other doctors' talents.

401
00:24:46,885 --> 00:24:47,986
I'll support them.

402
00:24:49,721 --> 00:24:50,822
That's my role.

403
00:24:51,556 --> 00:24:54,426
It is something
that is required for a leader.

404
00:24:55,594 --> 00:24:56,628
So?

405
00:24:57,128 --> 00:24:57,996
So...

406
00:24:59,030 --> 00:25:00,799
- Do your best.
- Huh?

407
00:25:01,066 --> 00:25:03,969
Do your best...

408
00:25:08,740 --> 00:25:10,008
Cheering me up?

409
00:25:19,851 --> 00:25:21,486
Another way...

410
00:25:25,790 --> 00:25:29,227
I found a new place for you to work.

411
00:25:29,628 --> 00:25:31,696
Don't make a face like that.

412
00:25:33,331 --> 00:25:34,165
Hm.

413
00:25:34,699 --> 00:25:36,067
Thank you, Akira.

414
00:25:37,235 --> 00:25:39,638
How about a hot-pot dish
with everyone today?

415
00:25:42,307 --> 00:25:43,875
You're depressed.

416
00:25:44,676 --> 00:25:47,479
Ben Casey is worried, too.

417
00:25:49,881 --> 00:25:52,117
I'm sorry, Ben Casey.

418
00:25:53,418 --> 00:25:55,921
I know Michiko performs
selfish surgeries.

419
00:25:56,621 --> 00:25:59,824
But she gives you unreasonable orders

420
00:26:00,258 --> 00:26:02,727
because she trusts you, right?

421
00:26:06,331 --> 00:26:08,466
Surgeons overdepend on us.

422
00:26:09,401 --> 00:26:11,636
We're the ones that suffer.

423
00:26:19,778 --> 00:26:22,847
But I know.

424
00:26:24,683 --> 00:26:29,688
Dr. Daimon's selfishness always
saves the patient's lives.

425
00:26:35,660 --> 00:26:40,498
It's her exclusive patent
to feel she won't fail.

426
00:26:45,236 --> 00:26:47,005
Oh, Dr. Ebina.

427
00:26:48,940 --> 00:26:50,375
Hi, Jonouchi.

428
00:26:53,445 --> 00:26:54,579
Can you...

429
00:26:55,747 --> 00:26:58,416
What happened all of a sudden?

430
00:26:58,483 --> 00:27:01,252
I'm worried about you.

431
00:27:01,886 --> 00:27:03,488
I hope this helps to refresh you.

432
00:27:04,356 --> 00:27:07,058
Although a freelancer
you're still my co-worker.

433
00:27:07,592 --> 00:27:08,860
I couldn't leave you alone.

434
00:27:10,562 --> 00:27:11,963
I appreciate it.

435
00:27:12,497 --> 00:27:16,568
I think you are
the best anesthesiologist.

436
00:27:17,769 --> 00:27:20,438
Dr. Inomata is stupid to banish you.

437
00:27:21,272 --> 00:27:22,107
Yeah.

438
00:27:22,607 --> 00:27:26,978
Sooner or later I'll try to
get you back to the hospital.

439
00:27:27,679 --> 00:27:30,982
And I want you be at
all of my surgeries

440
00:27:31,616 --> 00:27:33,418
as my partner.

441
00:27:33,918 --> 00:27:36,554
- Partner?
- No, not like that.

442
00:27:36,821 --> 00:27:39,391
Surgeons and anesthesiologists
are partners, right?

443
00:27:41,059 --> 00:27:43,228
Anyway, let's order.

444
00:27:43,895 --> 00:27:46,164
You can eat whatever you want.
This is my treat.

445
00:27:48,533 --> 00:27:50,101
Such a cheap place.

446
00:27:51,069 --> 00:27:52,937
LUNCH MENU $9.18 FOR ONE PERSON

447
00:27:56,041 --> 00:27:56,875
Atsuko.

448
00:27:57,208 --> 00:28:00,578
Michiko is there for you.
You'll be all right.

449
00:28:00,979 --> 00:28:01,813
Yes.

450
00:28:04,649 --> 00:28:05,550
Do your best.

451
00:28:21,900 --> 00:28:24,069
Mr. Mutsuura! Mr. Mutsuura?

452
00:28:24,369 --> 00:28:25,470
Go get Dr. Inomata!

453
00:28:26,204 --> 00:28:29,574
You'll be all right.
The doctor will be here immediately.

454
00:28:37,048 --> 00:28:38,516
What about the retroperitoneum?

455
00:28:39,017 --> 00:28:41,553
Adhesiotomy keeping a large margin.

456
00:28:43,154 --> 00:28:44,155
Dr. Daimon.

457
00:28:44,489 --> 00:28:48,059
Mr. Mutsuura collapsed.
He'll have emergency surgery.

458
00:28:51,129 --> 00:28:52,897
I see. I'll be there soon.

459
00:28:54,966 --> 00:28:55,834
What's wrong?

460
00:28:56,234 --> 00:28:58,269
Mr. Mutsuura collapsed.

461
00:28:58,737 --> 00:29:00,405
He will have emergency surgery.

462
00:29:00,638 --> 00:29:02,707
His wife's surgery will begin, too.

463
00:29:03,374 --> 00:29:05,176
Maybe it'll be a simultaneous surgery.

464
00:29:05,710 --> 00:29:07,378
Sorry, I'll go back to the hospital.

465
00:29:10,515 --> 00:29:12,517
Is it okay to split the bill?

466
00:29:13,251 --> 00:29:14,119
Sorry.

467
00:29:15,019 --> 00:29:15,887
Please wait.

468
00:29:17,355 --> 00:29:18,723
I'll pay for everything.

469
00:29:19,190 --> 00:29:20,058
What?

470
00:29:21,226 --> 00:29:22,193
In exchange...

471
00:29:31,703 --> 00:29:34,439
EMERGENCY PANCREATICODUODENECTOMY

472
00:29:36,641 --> 00:29:38,476
Transverse colon resection. Kelly.

473
00:29:47,952 --> 00:29:48,820
Condition?

474
00:29:49,287 --> 00:29:51,823
Acute pancreatitis is causing GI bleeding.

475
00:29:52,257 --> 00:29:53,424
What are you going to do?

476
00:29:53,892 --> 00:29:55,794
Your plan can't save his life.

477
00:29:56,261 --> 00:29:57,462
None of your business.

478
00:29:58,229 --> 00:29:59,764
Just do your surgery.

479
00:30:00,932 --> 00:30:05,103
We need to start surgery.
Mrs. Mutsuura started general anesthesia.

480
00:30:16,548 --> 00:30:19,184
- So late, Dr. Daimon.
- I know.

481
00:30:24,389 --> 00:30:27,625
Dr. Jonouchi was suddenly
assigned to this surgery.

482
00:30:27,826 --> 00:30:30,528
I'm glad Dr. Ebina lifted her ban.

483
00:30:31,229 --> 00:30:32,130
Good.

484
00:30:32,430 --> 00:30:33,298
Do your best.

485
00:30:36,901 --> 00:30:39,404
Kin, what is the volume of potassium?

486
00:30:40,505 --> 00:30:42,140
Um…Kin?

487
00:30:43,208 --> 00:30:45,009
- Dr. Jonouchi, potassium?
- 4.5.

488
00:30:45,210 --> 00:30:47,312
- She said 4.5.
- Is the ECG normal?

489
00:30:49,881 --> 00:30:53,218
Kin, I'm asking you.
Is the ECG normal?

490
00:30:53,284 --> 00:30:54,319
Why me?

491
00:30:55,653 --> 00:30:56,955
Dr. Jonouchi, ECG?

492
00:30:57,021 --> 00:30:58,556
Pulse 72, normal sinus rhythm.

493
00:30:58,623 --> 00:31:00,425
Pulse 72, normal sinus rhythm.

494
00:31:00,625 --> 00:31:04,062
What's the matter?
Can't you talk to her?

495
00:31:04,128 --> 00:31:05,129
Change surgeon.

496
00:31:05,563 --> 00:31:07,198
- What?
- Change?

497
00:31:07,265 --> 00:31:09,734
We're starting.
What're you talking about?

498
00:31:10,268 --> 00:31:13,438
If that anesthesiologist is here,
I won't do surgery.

499
00:31:14,072 --> 00:31:15,740
Let's start. You are not a kid.

500
00:31:15,940 --> 00:31:17,508
Change to whom?

501
00:31:23,014 --> 00:31:24,582
- You.
- Me?

502
00:31:25,650 --> 00:31:27,852
I don't think he can handle this.
I'll do it.

503
00:31:28,319 --> 00:31:31,155
Only the ones who studied
and prepared can do the surgery.

504
00:31:32,724 --> 00:31:35,693
Minimum blood loss and
perfect hemostasis.

505
00:31:36,427 --> 00:31:37,262
Yes.

506
00:31:38,129 --> 00:31:39,364
Kin, support him.

507
00:31:39,430 --> 00:31:42,333
My name is Mamoru Hara.
Are you leaving for real?

508
00:31:53,378 --> 00:31:56,848
BP dropped. 58 over 35.
Pulse 135.

509
00:31:56,981 --> 00:31:59,450
I know. Hey, suction.

510
00:32:02,353 --> 00:32:03,688
Why is this happening to me?

511
00:32:04,188 --> 00:32:07,859
I can never report to the director
if he loses his life.

512
00:32:11,763 --> 00:32:12,931
Dr. Daimon.

513
00:32:13,131 --> 00:32:14,132
I see.

514
00:32:14,899 --> 00:32:15,767
I get it.

515
00:32:15,900 --> 00:32:17,735
- Why are you here?
- Move.

516
00:32:18,102 --> 00:32:19,304
How about your surgery?

517
00:32:20,071 --> 00:32:21,673
Did you leave your patient?

518
00:32:22,674 --> 00:32:23,675
He is my patient.

519
00:32:23,741 --> 00:32:25,243
I can't let you do it.

520
00:32:25,610 --> 00:32:27,612
Are you kidding? Back off!

521
00:32:28,713 --> 00:32:29,714
Change method.

522
00:32:30,515 --> 00:32:31,716
Total pancreatectomy!

523
00:32:32,917 --> 00:32:33,751
Hey!

524
00:32:34,185 --> 00:32:35,653
Stop being selfish.

525
00:32:36,187 --> 00:32:38,189
Are you ignoring the patient's request?

526
00:32:38,256 --> 00:32:40,658
The patient's request is
to save his life first!

527
00:32:45,763 --> 00:32:46,798
I quit.

528
00:32:47,031 --> 00:32:50,969
It's all your responsibility
if anything happens.

529
00:32:52,637 --> 00:32:56,240
I don't want to be involved in this.
I won't do this.

530
00:32:57,108 --> 00:33:00,478
Wait! How can we continue
without an anesthesiologist?!

531
00:33:01,813 --> 00:33:03,548
How about you, First Assistant?

532
00:33:04,115 --> 00:33:05,383
I'll stay here.

533
00:33:05,783 --> 00:33:06,985
Me, too.

534
00:33:07,318 --> 00:33:08,152
I'll do it, too.

535
00:33:08,519 --> 00:33:10,722
But we can't do it without
an anesthesiologist.

536
00:33:15,660 --> 00:33:17,128
Dr. Daimon, what should we do?

537
00:33:18,663 --> 00:33:20,331
I can handle anesthesia.

538
00:33:24,102 --> 00:33:25,036
Really?

539
00:33:26,337 --> 00:33:28,673
Increase dopamine and
add blood transfusion.

540
00:33:28,940 --> 00:33:30,408
Administer catecholamine.

541
00:33:30,475 --> 00:33:32,677
Once the vital stabilizes,
hemostasis.

542
00:33:33,144 --> 00:33:34,579
I'll remove the tumor.

543
00:33:35,480 --> 00:33:36,781
Daimon, are you kidding?

544
00:33:52,563 --> 00:33:54,499
Dissecting right kidney.

545
00:34:04,709 --> 00:34:05,643
Really?

546
00:34:06,411 --> 00:34:07,278
So fast.

547
00:34:08,079 --> 00:34:10,581
SURGERY TIME

548
00:34:10,648 --> 00:34:14,152
Dissecting renal veins first
increases blood loss.

549
00:34:14,218 --> 00:34:17,989
So ligate it first before
its actual ligature and excision.

550
00:34:18,122 --> 00:34:19,690
I'll do the proximal.

551
00:34:19,824 --> 00:34:21,492
1-0 silk.

552
00:34:25,563 --> 00:34:28,299
Leave the hemodynamics to me.
I'll handle it.

553
00:34:42,013 --> 00:34:43,614
5-0 absorbable.

554
00:34:45,349 --> 00:34:48,419
Dr. Daimon, the results of
the resection margin.

555
00:34:56,794 --> 00:34:57,762
Okay. Thanks.

556
00:35:03,968 --> 00:35:04,802
Dr. Daimon?

557
00:35:06,404 --> 00:35:08,372
It is not malignant.

558
00:35:10,541 --> 00:35:12,977
Dr. Daimon. What?
We have to do this.

559
00:35:13,878 --> 00:35:15,313
Daimon, what's wrong?

560
00:35:23,788 --> 00:35:25,623
Change method again.

561
00:35:25,756 --> 00:35:26,591
What?

562
00:35:26,657 --> 00:35:28,059
5-0 absorbable.

563
00:35:28,793 --> 00:35:30,194
What do you mean
change method?

564
00:35:30,695 --> 00:35:32,697
If you connect the pancreatic body
to the stomach,

565
00:35:32,763 --> 00:35:34,065
we won't have to remove it.

566
00:35:35,233 --> 00:35:37,268
Middle-segment-preserving
pancreatectomy.

567
00:35:37,502 --> 00:35:40,338
It's impossible to change the method
at this point.

568
00:35:40,404 --> 00:35:41,339
No anesthesiologist!

569
00:35:41,405 --> 00:35:42,740
We have to do it.

570
00:35:43,441 --> 00:35:45,042
Get ready for pancreatic duct tube.

571
00:35:45,276 --> 00:35:48,379
Hey, Assistant. Increase dopamine.

572
00:35:55,486 --> 00:35:56,687
Dr. Jonouchi!

573
00:35:57,288 --> 00:35:58,789
You are late.

574
00:35:59,023 --> 00:36:00,992
I only have one body.

575
00:36:01,692 --> 00:36:03,027
Vital seems stable.

576
00:36:03,461 --> 00:36:05,830
It's managed by the dopamine.
Increase it.

577
00:36:05,997 --> 00:36:07,598
Changed the method, right?

578
00:36:07,832 --> 00:36:09,333
Preserving the pancreatic body.

579
00:36:09,500 --> 00:36:12,803
There's no need for insulin
and QOL rises.

580
00:36:13,070 --> 00:36:16,140
I think you know but
this is high risk.

581
00:36:17,441 --> 00:36:20,244
I never fail.

582
00:36:23,381 --> 00:36:26,517
BP 136 over 92.
Pulse 85.

583
00:36:30,888 --> 00:36:34,091
Leaving the center
and resecting the tumor.

584
00:36:35,126 --> 00:36:36,827
And preserving the pancreas function.

585
00:36:38,296 --> 00:36:39,564
Is it possible?

586
00:36:44,502 --> 00:36:48,706
Did you lift her ban without
my permission?

587
00:36:49,674 --> 00:36:51,275
To save Mr. and Mrs. Mutsuura.

588
00:36:51,776 --> 00:36:56,013
Daimon could come here because
Jonouchi was at his wife's surgery.

589
00:36:56,380 --> 00:36:57,381
I don't care.

590
00:36:57,848 --> 00:36:59,650
This method is impossible.

591
00:37:02,453 --> 00:37:06,490
If they fail you are fired.

592
00:37:12,263 --> 00:37:14,599
Incision of gastric wall.
Monopolar.

593
00:37:14,665 --> 00:37:15,633
SURGERY TIME

594
00:37:15,700 --> 00:37:16,834
Hurry up!

595
00:37:17,134 --> 00:37:19,303
- Time left to finish the operation?
- 30 minutes.

596
00:37:19,570 --> 00:37:21,205
- Don't worry.
- Okay.

597
00:37:34,719 --> 00:37:35,653
Incredible!

598
00:37:47,798 --> 00:37:48,699
Finished.

599
00:37:48,899 --> 00:37:52,737
BP 132 over 84.
Pulse 76, normal sinus rhythm.

600
00:38:01,946 --> 00:38:03,981
I'll be looking forward to
eating your gyoza.

601
00:38:09,587 --> 00:38:12,556
Good job...

602
00:38:12,623 --> 00:38:13,791
You, too.

603
00:38:23,868 --> 00:38:25,303
Yay! She did it!

604
00:38:38,849 --> 00:38:41,185
Thank you. You did a fantastic job!

605
00:38:41,585 --> 00:38:43,621
Thanks for doing me this favor.

606
00:38:43,688 --> 00:38:46,691
I've let you come back and
we've saved them both.

607
00:38:46,757 --> 00:38:47,725
I'm very happy.

608
00:38:48,859 --> 00:38:51,262
Partnerships are nice.

609
00:38:52,129 --> 00:38:54,498
Yes, they are.

610
00:38:54,832 --> 00:38:57,802
Let's go out to eat again.
I know a good restaurant.

611
00:39:00,237 --> 00:39:01,105
I'm sorry.

612
00:39:01,972 --> 00:39:05,009
My partner is waiting for me.

613
00:39:05,509 --> 00:39:06,944
- Excuse me.
- Huh?

614
00:39:07,411 --> 00:39:08,879
Goodbye.

615
00:39:08,946 --> 00:39:12,850
I'm going on a business trip to Yamanashi.
I want you to come with me!

616
00:39:13,351 --> 00:39:14,752
You are my partner, right?

617
00:39:19,223 --> 00:39:21,092
Excuse me.

618
00:39:21,158 --> 00:39:22,026
Dr. Daimon.

619
00:39:28,599 --> 00:39:29,734
Dr. Daimon, I...

620
00:39:30,568 --> 00:39:33,504
Thank you for letting me
handle the surgery.

621
00:39:34,004 --> 00:39:34,905
Don't thank me.

622
00:39:35,606 --> 00:39:38,843
Dr. Jonouchi and Kin were there
so I thought there'd be no problem.

623
00:39:41,045 --> 00:39:42,012
I see.

624
00:39:45,282 --> 00:39:47,118
Minimum blood loss.

625
00:39:47,618 --> 00:39:50,688
No problems with the amount of
moisture and electrolyte.

626
00:39:52,390 --> 00:39:53,691
Perfect surgery.

627
00:39:55,960 --> 00:39:56,927
I'm honored.

628
00:39:57,795 --> 00:39:58,896
Thank you.

629
00:40:08,072 --> 00:40:09,573
Excuse me.

630
00:40:11,842 --> 00:40:13,077
Rewards.

631
00:40:16,414 --> 00:40:18,616
You are here, Dr. Inomata.

632
00:40:19,984 --> 00:40:21,519
Who are you?

633
00:40:21,952 --> 00:40:24,288
In the director's absence,

634
00:40:24,555 --> 00:40:29,160
I'd like to give this to
the acting director.

635
00:40:29,960 --> 00:40:30,961
Melon.

636
00:40:32,463 --> 00:40:33,898
The bill.

637
00:40:37,468 --> 00:40:39,904
What's this?
This is ridiculous.

638
00:40:40,237 --> 00:40:45,576
As for Jonouchi,
we're charging for two surgeries.

639
00:40:46,343 --> 00:40:49,046
That's why I don't like part-timers.

640
00:40:49,146 --> 00:40:51,715
She is such a gold digger.

641
00:40:54,218 --> 00:40:56,554
If we pay you this amount,

642
00:40:57,555 --> 00:41:02,626
we need a corresponding report
to be made to the director.

643
00:41:03,894 --> 00:41:07,565
For example, we performed
simultaneous surgery for the couple.

644
00:41:07,932 --> 00:41:12,036
Miraculously, what seemed like
an impossible case was a success.

645
00:41:12,536 --> 00:41:14,438
The surgeon was...

646
00:41:16,941 --> 00:41:21,245
You let me take your credit and
claim hush money?

647
00:41:21,378 --> 00:41:22,246
No.

648
00:41:22,947 --> 00:41:29,053
This time please write Michiko Daimon
and Hiromi Jonouchi's name.

649
00:41:29,887 --> 00:41:30,721
What?

650
00:41:31,121 --> 00:41:32,122
In exchange

651
00:41:32,957 --> 00:41:36,494
I can make a discount of
excluding the hush money.

652
00:41:37,628 --> 00:41:38,629
$5.

653
00:41:40,598 --> 00:41:41,999
What do you mean?

654
00:41:42,933 --> 00:41:49,340
I have an uncanny impression
about what he said earlier.

655
00:41:57,047 --> 00:41:58,115
What?

656
00:41:58,549 --> 00:42:03,721
You abandoned the surgery and
put the patient's life in danger.

657
00:42:04,655 --> 00:42:06,757
You've left the patient to die.

658
00:42:06,891 --> 00:42:10,594
Don't you dare
make a fool out of Jonouchi.

659
00:42:17,835 --> 00:42:23,073
Will you report on the surgeon and
the anesthesiologist who abandoned

660
00:42:23,941 --> 00:42:25,676
the operation in the middle of it?

661
00:42:33,150 --> 00:42:35,219
Uri, get out.

662
00:42:36,620 --> 00:42:38,289
Well, see you later.

663
00:42:38,722 --> 00:42:39,590
No.

664
00:42:40,925 --> 00:42:42,192
From this hospital.

665
00:42:44,461 --> 00:42:45,863
You're fired.

666
00:42:58,842 --> 00:43:02,947
This time we got a deal.

667
00:43:04,214 --> 00:43:05,916
Thank you so much.

668
00:43:13,591 --> 00:43:16,860
Akira is late.

669
00:43:17,127 --> 00:43:19,830
Hey, don't touch me.
What are you doing?

670
00:43:20,698 --> 00:43:22,866
A big success!

671
00:43:23,067 --> 00:43:24,868
I got it!

672
00:43:25,002 --> 00:43:27,471
He's coming.
It seems like it went well.

673
00:43:27,538 --> 00:43:31,308
From today I'll run on
a commission system.

674
00:43:32,076 --> 00:43:35,512
I'm telling you, you might get less
depending on the condition.

675
00:43:35,579 --> 00:43:37,247
Really? What should I do?

676
00:43:37,381 --> 00:43:39,183
Negotiate yourself.

677
00:43:39,249 --> 00:43:40,217
- Stingy.
- Hey.

678
00:43:40,618 --> 00:43:42,519
Don't, not with the big bag of yours.

679
00:43:42,586 --> 00:43:44,188
No. Your furry bag...

680
00:43:44,254 --> 00:43:48,258
Thank you! Coming through...

681
00:43:48,325 --> 00:43:49,360
Akira.

682
00:43:49,426 --> 00:43:53,497
<i>Despising the herd mentality, authority</i>
<i>and institutional restraints...</i>

683
00:43:53,864 --> 00:43:59,169
<i>Her solo weapons are her license</i>
<i>and the skills she has acquired.</i>

684
00:44:00,437 --> 00:44:02,573
CHINESE GYOZA

685
00:44:02,640 --> 00:44:05,909
Ahh, the gyoza is ready now!

686
00:44:08,245 --> 00:44:13,917
How happy I am
to be well and cooking gyoza.

687
00:44:13,984 --> 00:44:14,885
Thank you.

688
00:44:15,519 --> 00:44:19,757
You won a gyoza championship, right?

689
00:44:19,990 --> 00:44:21,425
It was three years ago.

690
00:44:21,492 --> 00:44:24,628
Great! Was there a cash award?

691
00:44:24,695 --> 00:44:26,830
It's not a big deal.

692
00:44:28,632 --> 00:44:29,466
It was $5,000.

693
00:44:30,567 --> 00:44:32,636
$5,000? It was $3,000, right?

694
00:44:34,605 --> 00:44:36,740
Was it $5,000?

695
00:44:36,807 --> 00:44:37,641
No, no...

696
00:44:37,708 --> 00:44:39,076
What did you spend $2,000 on?

697
00:44:40,711 --> 00:44:44,014
Hostess bar...

698
00:44:44,581 --> 00:44:47,785
I'm so disappointed with you!

699
00:44:48,185 --> 00:44:49,319
Don't touch me.

700
00:44:49,386 --> 00:44:52,523
You've been lying to me all this while.

701
00:44:52,856 --> 00:44:54,958
Don't touch me, dirty old man!

702
00:44:55,025 --> 00:44:55,859
Wait!

703
00:44:57,428 --> 00:44:58,529
She is scary.

704
00:44:58,929 --> 00:45:01,165
Everyone gets into trouble
when money is involved.

705
00:45:01,231 --> 00:45:03,834
Are my gyoza ready yet?

706
00:45:04,201 --> 00:45:06,537
<i>Surgeon Michiko Daimon.</i>

707
00:45:07,438 --> 00:45:08,272
<i>Also known as...</i>

708
00:45:08,706 --> 00:45:10,407
<i>Doctor-X.</i>

709
00:45:10,474 --> 00:45:12,576
THIS DRAMA IS FICTION

710
00:45:12,643 --> 00:45:13,544
Hurry up.

711
00:45:14,645 --> 00:45:16,880
- Mamoru!
- Who are you?

712
00:45:16,947 --> 00:45:18,048
Kin's girlfriend.

713
00:45:18,115 --> 00:45:20,417
- You're mistaken.
- Excuse me?

714
00:45:20,551 --> 00:45:23,020
You'll ruin your career forever.

715
00:45:23,087 --> 00:45:24,154
I want to save her.

716
00:45:25,322 --> 00:45:26,957
Saving her life is more important.

717
00:45:27,124 --> 00:45:28,592
Don't underestimate operations.
